@startuml async-poll-record-lifecycle
' Lifecycle of one kaalm-async-{requestId} ConfigMap as a poller sees it.
' Each state carries only the status a poll returns. The events, the TTL
' rules, and the signals are the prose on
' docs/src/gateways/api/async-responses.md (the source of truth).
!include _style.puml

state "Absent" as Absent $mutedBg
state "Placeholder" as Placeholder
state "Patched" as Patched
state "Expired" as Expired $mutedBg

Absent : **404**
Placeholder : **202**
Patched : **200**
Expired : **404**

[*] --> Absent
Absent --> Placeholder : Create
Placeholder --> Patched : Patch
Placeholder -[#B71C1C]-> Expired : 1h from Create\n(no Patch)
Patched --> Expired : 1h from Create
Expired -up-> Absent : prune
Placeholder -up-> Absent : sweep
Patched -up-> Absent : sweep
@enduml
